{
  "assessment": "The source packet provides a complete manuscript with main text and supplementary information. The selected quantitative cluster is the finite-temperature critical quench dynamics of primary fields, with the first-order conformal perturbation theory result (Eq. g^1) and the second-order result (Eq. g^2) as the two regimes. The controls are the perturbation strength g and time t; the readout is the expectation value of the primary field. The source provides explicit scaling forms, universal constants, and applicability conditions (beta J >> 1, 2 pi t >> beta). The extraction is case_authoring_ready because there is at least one numeric control (g), one numeric readout (langle Phi(t) rangle), a quantitative mechanism (conformal perturbation theory), and an objective source-grounded response within an explicit domain.",
